insert into public.problems (id, title, source, url, difficulty_rating, statement_md, input_format_md, output_format_md, constraints_text, sample_io, target_complexity) values ('uva-10090', 'Custo das caixas', 'UVA', 'https://vjudge.net/problem/UVA-10090', 1500, '10090         Marbles
I have some (say, n) marbles (small glass balls) and I am going to buy some boxes to store them. The
boxes are of two types:

T ype 1: each box costs c1 Taka and can hold exactly n1 marbles

T ype 2: each box costs c2 Taka and can hold exactly n2 marbles

    I want each of the used boxes to be filled to its capacity and also to minimize the total cost of buying
them. Since I find it difficult for me to figure out how to distribute my marbles among the boxes, I
seek your help. I want your program to be efficient also.

Input
The input file may contain multiple test cases. Each test case begins with a line containing the integer
n (1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000). The second line contains c1 and n1 , and the third line contains c2 and n2 .
Here, c1 , c2 , n1 and n2 are all positive integers having values smaller than 2,000,000,000.
   A test case containing a zero for n in the first line terminates the input.

Output
For each test case in the input print a line containing the minimum cost solution (two nonnegative
integers m1 and m2 , where mi = number of T ypei boxes required) if one exists, print ‘failed’ otherwise.
    If a solution exists, you may assume that it is unique.

Sample Input
43
1 3
2 4
40
5 9
5 12
0

Sample Output
13 1
failed

_Source: PDF text extraction — figures/diagrams may be missing; verify against the original._', 'The input file may contain multiple test cases. Each test case begins with a line containing the integer
n (1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000). The second line contains c1 and n1 , and the third line contains c2 and n2 .
Here, c1 , c2 , n1 and n2 are all positive integers having values smaller than 2,000,000,000.
   A test case containing a zero for n in the first line terminates the input.', 'For each test case in the input print a line containing the minimum cost solution (two nonnegative
integers m1 and m2 , where mi = number of T ypei boxes required) if one exists, print ‘failed’ otherwise.
    If a solution exists, you may assume that it is unique.', '(1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000)', '[{"input":"The input file may contain multiple test cases. Each test case begins with a line containing the integer\nn (1 ≤ n ≤ 2, 000, 000, 000). The second line contains c1 and n1 , and the third line contains c2 and n2 .\nHere, c1 , c2 , n1 and n2 are all positive integers having values smaller than 2,000,000,000.\n   A test case containing a zero for n in the first line terminates the input.","output":"For each test case in the input print a line containing the minimum cost solution (two nonnegative\nintegers m1 and m2 , where mi = number of T ypei boxes required) if one exists, print ‘failed’ otherwise.\n    If a solution exists, you may assume that it is unique."}]'::jsonb, 'O(N log N)');
